course: dictionary
lesson: 15514
title: Subsequent: what comes after
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Subsequent is a formal word. It means coming after something else, in time or order. Its clue is the word sequence, which is a list of things that follow one another. So subsequent means later or following.
explain: «The school trip was cancelled. In subsequent years, the children went to the zoo instead.» The word years is your clue: the zoo trips came after the cancelled trip. Try it: "in the years that followed" fits, so subsequent means later.
explain: You will often see subsequent to, which means after. «Subsequent to the storm, the power was off for three days.» Swap in after: "after the storm, the power was off" still makes sense, so subsequent to means after.
fact: Subsequent means coming after something else in time or order.
fact: Subsequent is a formal word, often found in reports, letters and exams.
fact: «Subsequent» is used in maths sequences, where each subsequent term follows the one before.
fact: «Subsequent to» means after, as in «subsequent to the match».
fact: Subsequent comes from the same family as sequence, a set of things in order.
exercise: «The first game was a draw. In the subsequent game, Ravi scored three goals.» What does subsequent mean here? | *Coming after, the next one | Coming before the first game | Muddy and wet | Cancelled
exercise: Which phrase means after? | *subsequent to | at the table | very soon | in the morning
exercise: Why would a report use «subsequent events» instead of «later events»? | Because later is a rude word | Because events are always sad | *Because subsequent is a formal word for things that happened afterwards | Because subsequent means before
test: «Each subsequent day was warmer than the one before.» What does each subsequent day mean? | *Every day that came after | A day with no sun | Only the first day | The coldest day of the week
test: Which word could replace subsequent in «subsequent years»? | *following | earlier | silent | broken
exam: In the sentence «Subsequent to the bell, the children lined up», what does subsequent to mean? | *After the bell | Before the bell | Instead of the bell | During the lesson
